       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-28 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Amazon hosts NYC event to showcase new Echo hardware</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Amazon shifted from its traditional large fall hardware showcase to a series of smaller product launches throughout October. Recent releases include new Fire TV devices, Kindles, the Alexa Tablet Pro 12, Ring’s first smart lock, Blink 4K cameras, and hardware from the startup Bee.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/amazon-hosts-nyc-event-to-showcase-new-echo-hardware.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following these announcements, Amazon held a small event in New York City’s financial district this week to feature its latest Echo hardware. Senior vice president Panos Panay addressed attendees, emphasizing the company’s focus on launching meaningful products across its device portfolio.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the shift in Amazon's hardware launch strategy and the recent NYC event.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1020388/inside-amazons-echo-hardware-event" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
