     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-28 · editor 9/10 · 3 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Anthropic Launches Tools to Detail AI Spending Value for Enterprise Customers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#AI</span> <span>#Anthropic</span> <span>#Enterprise AI</span> <span>#Claude Code</span></div>
       <p>Anthropic, a frontier AI lab, has launched a new suite of reporting tools designed to provide companies with a more granular understanding of the value derived from their AI spending. This move comes as the company prepares for a planned IPO, lifting the curtain on how users spend money on its models. The tools aim to address a significant concern among large customers regarding the return on investment of AI deployments.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/anthropic-launches-tools-to-detail-ai-spending-value-for-ent.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The introduction of these tools follows strong financial performance for Anthropic. Financial data shared with investors indicated an operating profit in the second quarter, alongside an impressive 900% net revenue retention from Q3 2025 to Q3 2026 for its AI coding tool, Claude Code. The new reporting features allow managers to use internal analytics and employee surveys to view a team’s work, production output, associated costs, and identify workflow breakdowns over specific date ranges. Anthropic has stated that this data will not be used for model training by default, and the reports will also offer recommendations for improving results. Furthermore, Anthropic is establishing pooled group budgets to assist teams in better managing their token spending.</p><p>The broader industry context highlights a strong demand for such insights. While usage among venture-backed firms fuels token spend, many Fortune 500 companies are still struggling to realize major gains from their AI deployments. A recent report from Jellyfish, a company specializing in tools for software developers, based on 276,000 of its customers, underscored the prevalence of Anthropic's offerings. Claude Code and other tools built on Anthropic models remain the most widely used agentic coding tools in their survey, accounting for nearly a third of all proposed code changes submitted for review. Importantly, spending on these tools has surged tenfold since the beginning of the year, now representing approximately 2% of total engineering costs.</p><p>Nicholas Arcolano, the chief scientist at Jellyfish, commented to TechCrunch on this rapid growth, stating, &quot;Even if you’re saying 2% is still small, that 10x growth is growth that most CFOs didn’t plan for.&quot; He added, &quot;We’re certainly getting to the point where people are realizing, okay, it’s not enough to just spend a bunch. You now have to optimize it, make it work.&quot; The new Anthropic reports directly address this optimization challenge.</p><p>Despite the release of OpenAI’s Astra model this summer, which was seen as a potential threat, Anthropic's adoption numbers have not slowed. Nikolas Albarran, AI product lead at Jellyfish, observed that &quot;Anthropic was just there with great enterprise motions, and they had an incumbent weight of their own—this stuff just worked and worked well, and a lot of people just put a lot of effort into standardizing workflows around it. And there’s not a big enough reason to switch.&quot; The reality of business creates significant switching costs once a frontier lab is embedded with a customer, making transitions harder compared to individual programmers. Major AI labs are investing in forward-deployed engineering (FDE) organizations to embed consultants with customers, and these new reporting tools can be seen as a &quot;FDE-lite&quot; version of that hands-on support. Albarran concluded, &quot;We’re at a point now where it’s mature enough, where once you’re in, it’s going to be harder and harder to switch because you’ve spent the effort.&quot;</p><p>What to watch: How these tools influence enterprise AI adoption and spending optimization.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft successfully synthesizes the business context and technical details from the source while maintaining a professional tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/28/anthropic-just-launched-tools-to-show-companies-what-their-ai-spending-is-buying/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
