     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-28 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Apple's 'Pro and Tell' Event to Unveil Potential Touchscreen MacBook Amidst Recent Launches</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#The Verge</span> <span>#Apple</span> <span>#Pro and tell event</span> <span>#MacBook</span></div>
       <p>Apple's highly anticipated &quot;Pro and tell&quot; event is scheduled to commence at 1PM ET / 10AM PT on October 28th. This event follows a period of significant product introductions from the tech giant. Just weeks prior, Apple debuted the HomeView, marking its entry into the smart display market, and a little over a month ago, it unveiled the iPhone Duo, its inaugural foldable device. Speculation suggests the upcoming event could feature yet another &quot;first&quot; for Apple: a MacBook equipped with a touchscreen.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/apples-pro-and-tell-event-to-unveil-potential-touchscreen-ma.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In the days leading up to the &quot;Pro and tell&quot; event, Apple has already rolled out updates for several key devices. On Monday, the company announced an updated iPad Mini, which now boasts a larger OLED display. The following day, Tuesday, saw refreshes for both the iMac and the entry-level MacBook Pro, with both devices now featuring the new M6 chips. While these updated models are expected to make an appearance at Wednesday's event, their early announcement seemingly sets the stage for the potential touchscreen MacBook to take center stage.</p><p>The October 28th event continues a robust streak of product launches that began since John Ternus assumed the role of Apple's CEO on September 1st. Under his leadership, the company has introduced a rapid succession of new devices, including the iPhone 18 Pro, new Apple Watches, the AirPods 5, and the HomePod Mini 2. Apple's Greg Joswiak further heightened anticipation by teasing an &quot;exciting week&quot; ahead of the event.</p><p>What to watch: The potential unveiling of a touchscreen MacBook and further details on the M6 chip's capabilities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithfully incorporates all products, dates, timelines, and leadership context from the source article.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1018096/apple-pro-and-tell-launch-event-news-announcements" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
