       <h1>Bangladesh loses two wickets in opening session of Dhaka Test</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Bangladesh opted to bat first in the Dhaka Test against the West Indies on day one. West Indies handed a debut to Bishop, while veteran Mushfiqur Rahim was ruled out of the match due to a contusion injury.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/bangladesh-loses-two-wickets-in-opening-session-of-dhaka-tes.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In the opening session, West Indies bowlers Jayden Seales and Jomel Warrican each claimed a wicket to put early pressure on the hosts. Shadman Islam remained firm at the crease for Bangladesh, despite the team's early losses. The match follows discussions regarding Bangladesh's World Test Championship chances and the team's preparation for the series.</p>
