     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>CTI urges Rahul Gandhi to postpone INDIA bloc rally over trade concerns</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Chamber of Trade and Industry (CTI) has requested a meeting with Congress leader Rahul Gandhi to discuss the potential economic impact of the INDIA bloc's November 1 rally in Delhi. CTI chairman Brijesh Goyal warned that the event, expected to draw 10 lakh attendees, could disrupt business for 15 lakh traders during the peak Deepavali festive season.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/cti-urges-rahul-gandhi-to-postpone-india-bloc-rally-over-tra.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This marks the second time in four days that the CTI has urged a postponement of the event. The organization, representing 20 major markets including Chandni Chowk and Sadar Bazar, seeks to avoid a projected 10,000 crore trade loss, advocating for a dialogue to protect local commerce.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the CTI's concerns and the context of the rally.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Delhi/cti-writes-to-rahul-gandhi-again-on-india-blocs-nov-1-rally-amid-diwali/article71634413.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
