     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-28 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Education Leaders to Discuss AI and Skilling in Mumbai</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Skilling</span> <span>#Mumbai Conference</span></div>
       <p>Education sector leaders and policymakers are set to convene at a conference in Mumbai to discuss critical topics shaping the future of learning and employment. The gathering will focus on the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) within classrooms.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/education-leaders-to-discuss-ai-and-skilling-in-mumbai.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Key discussions will also revolve around strategies for skilling and upskilling the workforce to meet the demands of an evolving job market. This initiative, reported by ThePrint, underscores the growing importance of technology and relevant skills in the education landscape.</p><p>The Mumbai conference aims to bring together influential figures to formulate approaches for leveraging AI for educational advancement and ensuring that individuals are equipped with necessary competencies for future careers.</p><p>What to watch: Outcomes from the Mumbai conference on AI integration in education.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate but thin, as it relies on a very brief source summary. It covers the essential points without inventing additional details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
