     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Election Commission appoints 11 nodal officers for Manipur polls</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Election Commission has appointed 11 nodal officers to manage the upcoming 2027 Manipur Assembly elections. IPS officer Kamei Angam Romanus will oversee law and order and security, while IAS officer Hungyo Worshang is tasked with excise.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/election-commission-appoints-11-nodal-officers-for-manipur-p.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Additional officers were assigned to handle election expenditure, transport, and cyber security. The appointments follow recent visits by Election Commission officials to assess poll preparedness across the state's 16 districts. The assembly elections are tentatively expected to be held in February or March next year.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and covers the relevant officer appointments and context provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
