       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-10-28 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Japan Eyes Indian Firing Ranges for Missile and Drone Training</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Japan</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Defence Cooperation</span> <span>#Missile Training</span></div>
       <p>Japan is reportedly considering the use of Indian live firing ranges for training involving missiles and drones. This move signals a deepening of defence cooperation between the two nations, as reported by The Economic Times.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/japan-eyes-indian-firing-ranges-for-missile-and-drone-traini.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The potential utilization of Indian facilities would provide Japan with critical grounds for enhancing its military training capabilities, specifically in the areas of missile and drone operations. This development comes amid ongoing efforts to strengthen bilateral defence ties.</p><p>Such cooperation underscores a strategic alignment between Japan and India, aiming to foster greater interoperability and shared security interests in the region.</p><p>What to watch: Further developments in India-Japan defence training collaborations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a concise and accurate reflection of the provided source summary regarding India-Japan defence cooperation.</p>
