     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-28 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jio Platforms Soars on Debut, Reshaping Market Capitalization Hierarchy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Jio Platforms</span> <span>#Stock Market</span> <span>#IPO</span> <span>#Market Capitalisation</span></div>
       <p>Jio Platforms made a notable debut on the stock market Wednesday, rising 26.7 percent above its issue price to become India's second-most valuable listed company. The digital and telecommunications business opened at ₹1,358 apiece on the BSE and National Stock Exchange, a 21.4 percent premium over its ₹1,119 issue price. Shares closed at ₹1,417.35 on the BSE and ₹1,417.50 on the NSE, valuing Jio Platforms at ₹13.05 trillion. This valuation represents approximately 83 percent of parent Reliance Industries' market value and helped Mukesh Ambani's conglomerate surpass the Tata group in gross market capitalization, with the Ambani group's listed companies valued at ₹30.25 trillion against Tata's ₹25.40 trillion. Jio also overtook rival Bharti Airtel, whose shares fell 1.55 percent to ₹1,948.10 apiece, valuing Airtel at ₹12.16 trillion, about 7 percent less than Jio.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/jio-platforms-soars-on-debut-reshaping-market-capitalization.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Globally, Jio Platforms, with a market value of roughly $137 billion, ranked fifth among telecom companies, behind China Mobile ($221 billion). The initial public offering (IPO) attracted significant demand, with bids reaching 22.19 times the shares on offer, and total demand across the public issue and anchor-investor placement exceeding ₹7.4 trillion. The company successfully raised ₹30,213 crore through the IPO. Despite the successful debut, Reliance Industries' shares fell 3.19 percent to ₹1,158, leaving its market capitalization at ₹15.67 trillion, within one percent of its 52-week low.</p><p>The listing marked a significant milestone and a generational handover for the Mukesh Ambani family. Akash Ambani, Managing Director of Jio Platforms and Chairman of Reliance Jio Infocomm, stated the company would continue Reliance's shareholder commitment for the next fifty years, crediting his father Mukesh Ambani and grandfather Dhirubhai Ambani. Mukesh Ambani, 69, expressed his dream for Jio Platforms to become one of the world's great technology companies. Isha Ambani, a Jio Platforms director, recalled Reliance's 1977 IPO and its vision for public participation, noting Jio Platforms' annual revenue of about $15.5 billion and earnings of $8 billion. Anant Ambani, also a director, described the listing as a public trust and credited Isha and Akash for the company's vision and execution. Beyond telecom, Jio aims for its next decade to encompass artificial intelligence, cloud computing, connected devices, satellite connectivity, and new digital services.</p><p>The listing also sets the stage for future developments in the Indian telecom sector. Analysts anticipate an imminent tariff hike, potentially around 15 percent. Motilal Oswal Financial Services analysts now project a 15 percent smartphone tariff hike from March 2027, adjusted from their earlier December 2026 forecast. Ambit Capital Research maintains its expectation of a 15 percent hike in December 2026, followed by biennial increases.</p><p>What to watch: The potential for tariff hikes and Jio Platforms' expansion into new digital technologies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft provides a comprehensive summary of the source, capturing financial data, executive statements, and analyst projections accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/markets/ipo/jio-platforms-soars-on-debut-recasting-market-capitalisation-leaderboard-126102801887_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
