     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka publishes final electoral roll after massive revision</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Karnataka has published its final electoral roll following the completion of a Special Intensive Revision (SIR) exercise. The initiative aimed to ensure a clean voter list by including all eligible citizens and removing ineligible names from the records.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/karnataka-publishes-final-electoral-roll-after-massive-revis.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>As a result of the revision, over 99.32 lakh names were removed from the state's electoral rolls. Constituency-wise voter lists are now accessible to the public on the Chief Electoral Officer’s website. The state government launched the project to maintain the integrity of the electorate.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief adheres to the source material and accurately reports the figure regarding the electoral roll revision.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/videos/karnatakas-final-electoral-roll-published-after-sir/article71630933.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
