       <h1>Rajnath Singh and Pete Hegseth Review India-US Defence Framework</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India-US</span> <span>#Defence</span> <span>#Rajnath Singh</span></div>
       <p>Defence Minister Rajnath Singh held a meeting with Pete Hegseth in the Philippines to discuss the ongoing progress of the India-US Defence Framework. According to reports from ANI News and Telangana Today, the two leaders conducted a review of the strategic partnership and the specific advancements made under the existing bilateral framework.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/rajnath-singh-and-pete-hegseth-review-india-us-defence-frame.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The discussions focused on evaluating the current standing and future trajectory of defence cooperation between the two nations. While specific hardware or policy shifts were not detailed in the summaries provided, the meeting underscores the continued engagement between India and the United States regarding their shared defence objectives.</p><p>What to watch: Future statements regarding specific framework milestones.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate and makes good use of the available summary information, though it is brief due to the limited nature of the source.</p>
