     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Two Killed in Truck-Motorcycle Collision at Gujarat Roadwork Site</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Two women died instantly after a speeding truck collided with their motorcycle on the Ahmedabad-Dakor highway in Gujarat’s Kheda district. The incident occurred near a pothole-repair site in Keshra village, where authorities are investigating allegations that necessary safety measures, such as warning signs and barricades, were absent.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-28/two-killed-in-truck-motorcycle-collision-at-gujarat-roadwork.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Local residents gathered at the scene following the loud impact, prompting a police response. The victims' bodies were transported to a hospital for post-mortem examinations as legal proceedings began. Authorities are continuing to investigate the specific circumstances surrounding the fatal collision.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the incident, the location, and the ongoing investigation into safety measures.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/two-women-die-in-crash-near-road-repair-work-on-gujarat-highway-3027313-2026-10-29?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
